                <head>No. 387.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">General Sickles to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Received Feb. 14—10 a.m.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-02-12"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 12,
                        1873</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Castelar said to me to-night, with much feeling, that the Spanish Republic looked
                    especially to our Government and people for sympathy and support, and inquired
                    with solicitude whether our recognition would be delayed.</p>
                <p>President and cabinet entered on their duties at quarter past 2 this morning.
                    Cortes adjourned till this afternoon.</p>
                <p>Madrid is illuminated.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>SICKLES.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
